data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"The gradient for a batch is the average of the per-row gradients in that batch, so a smaller batch\ngives a noisier but cheaper step. Shuffling decides which rows share a batch, so it decides the\nsteps. The protocol fixes the order of the random draws, which is why the seed matters."},"hints_note":null}

