data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Build one generator with `default_rng(seed)` before the epoch loop. Each epoch, draw\n`perm = rng.permutation(n)`, then walk `range(0, n, batch_size)` and take `perm[start:start+batch_size]`.\nFor each slice, the gradient is `X_b.T @ (X_b @ w - y_b) / len(rows)`, and the update is `w - lr * g`.\nDivide by the slice's own length, not by `batch_size`, because the last slice can be shorter."},"hints_note":null}

